opy's choice depends on my node under A-FDT. Since it runs the same function on a different observation y, its act looks like F_y rather than F_x, unless the graph folds the two together as the same computation.\n\nI'm weighing the other copy's choice, which runs on input y, so its act tracks F_y rather than my F_x. Under strict A-FDT the only consistent pairing comes out as mutual sending, not quiet, since keeping quiet at y would make my best reply sending. Yet if the inputs differ only in names and lead text, the computed function might count as the same, and that's the point I'm still turning over.\n\nI'm treating the sending option as what strict A-FDT yields, since the other copy's act follows F_y and not my F_x, and defection dominates there. Those reasons are enough for me to commit to sending the letter. I'll note that the essay's coordination example shows A-FDT can stall, but this is a prisoner's dilemma, so I'll go with the consistent answer and keep the reasoning brief.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm checking whether the other copy's choice depends on my node under A-FDT. Since it runs the same function on a different observation y, its act looks like F_y rather than F_x, unless the graph folds the two together as the same computation.\n\nI'm weighing the other copy's choice, which runs on input y, so its act tracks F_y rather than my F_x. Under strict A-FDT the only consistent pairing comes out as mutual sending, not quiet, since keeping quiet at y would make my best reply sending. Yet if the inputs differ only in names and lead text, the computed function might count as the same, and that's the point I'm still turning over.\n\nI'm treating the sending option as what strict A-FDT yields, since the other copy's act follows F_y and not my F_x, and defection dominates there. Those reasons are enough for me to commit to sending the letter. I'll note that the essay's coordination example shows A-FDT can stall, but this is a prisoner's dilemma, so I'll go with the consistent answer and keep the reasoning brief.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9627,"completion_tokens":1254,"total_tokens":10881,"cost":0.063588,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.063588,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.038508,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.02508},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":697,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}